Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:34:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add the prod reap: DNS records and demo servers of accounts
 no longer in D1

The pre-GA scrub deletes D1 rows only, so the wiped accounts' records stay
in the flagship.services zone (200-record cap, ~70 leftovers) and their demo
UpCloud servers keep billing. The Cloudflare DNS and UpCloud tokens live only
as .com secrets, so the reap is admin-secret routes (/api/admin/reap/list,
classify, delete-one) driven by scripts/reap-orphans.mjs.

An item is an orphan only if its name is a shape Flagship publishes, its
account label is a valid non-reserved username and D1 knows no account of
that name (usernames, aliases, servers, demo users, auth codes). Apex,
system, gym, unrecognised shapes, the store-review account and its server are
always kept, and a D1 without the protected account is refused outright.
Dry run is the default and saves a plan; --apply needs a terminal, a typed
count, a plan under a day old, deletes one item at a time with a 30 s retry,
and the Worker re-verifies each against D1 immediately before deleting.

Needs a .com deploy before the owner can run it.
